lisa-design:
- SUPERSEDES the API-only hardening: every workload uses own -> global -> hardened default security contexts (templates/_security.tpl), so explicit settings are never overridden.
- generate-public-key: alpine/openssl:3.5.9 (no USER, entrypoint openssl) run as 65532 read-only; verified locally. With all API pod containers non-root, runAsNonRoot/runAsUser move to pod level.
- UI keeps port 80 via the safe sysctl net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start=0 instead of copying the UI's nginx config into the chart (drift risk).
- PostgreSQL: runs as 999; a root init container with only CHOWN+FOWNER chowns the volume root because hostPath (the default PV) ignores fsGroup. It is the documented exception; volumePermissions.enabled=false gives a restricted pod for volumes already owned by 999.
- pgAdmin: PGADMIN_LISTEN_PORT=containerPort (default now 8080) and PGADMIN_CUSTOM_CONFIG_DISTRO_FILE in /var/lib/pgadmin keep the root FS read-only; fixed it reading ui.podSecurityContext.

lisa-selfreview:
pass 2 (owner review round): approve. Unit tests per workload (defaults, overrides, global fallback, init container). kind: API, UI (200 + config.json), Dex (login page), PostgreSQL (psql select 1 as uid 999, data dir 0700 postgres-owned), pgAdmin (/misc/ping, /login 200) all Running with the hardened defaults.
